معنى قوله تعالى إن الله مع الصابرين هو إيجاب معيّة خاصة من الله عز وجل للصابرين [[qa:icadb-book:10282:71]]. هذه المعية تتضمن حفظهم ونصرهم وتأييدهم من قبل الله [[qa:icadb-book:10282:71]].

{{quran:8:46}}

توضح الآية الكريمة وجوب الالتزام بطاعة الله ورسوله في جميع الأحوال، والتحذير من الاختلاف الذي يؤدي إلى ضعف القوة وضياع النصر [[tafsir:muyassar:8:46]]. كما تأمر بالصبر عند مواجهة العدو، وتؤكد أن الله يكون مع الصابرين بالعون والنصر والتأييد، وأنه لن يخذلهم أبداً [[tafsir:muyassar:8:46]].

{{quran:8:66}}

ويشير تفسير الآية إلى أن الله يعين الصابرين بتأييده ونصره [[tafsir:muyassar:8:66]]. كما يقتضي لفظ مع في هذا السياق معنى النصرة [[term:icadb-yaseer:4867]].

Jihad is broadly defined as exerting one's full effort and capacity to defend Islam, its people, and its teachings [[qa:icadb:26100, term:icadb-yaseer:3121]]. It involves striving for the sake of Allāh by upholding His word, establishing justice on earth, and removing oppression or corruption [[qa:icadb-book:14:106]].

Scholars classify Jihad into several types, including the struggle against one's own self to learn and practice the religion while remaining patient through its difficulties [[qa:icadb-book:14:106]]. Other forms of striving include speaking the truth in the face of injustice or persisting in acts of worship like prayer and fasting [[hadith:hadeethenc:3045, hadith:hadeethenc:3485, qa:icadb:36193]].

In a broader sense, Jihad refers to any sincere action taken to seek closeness to Allāh by performing obligatory or voluntary acts [[qa:dorar-feqhia:2517:1]]. While the term is often associated with physical defense against those who attack Islam or its followers, it also encompasses the spiritual struggle of the soul [[qa:icadb:36193, qa:icadb-book:14:106]].

