Islam is built upon five fundamental pillars that serve as the basis for a Muslim's faith and religious practices [[qa:icadb-book:389:21, qa:icadb-book:382:17]]. These pillars are established to create an integrated system of worship and conduct [[qa:icadb-book:389:21]].

{{hadith:hadeethenc:65000}}

{{hadith:hadeethenc:66512}}

The five pillars are as follows:
1. The testimony of faith (Shahada), which involves believing that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muhammad is His messenger [[qa:icadb:36127, qa:icadb-book:382:17]].
2. Establishing prayer (Salah) [[qa:dorar-feqhia:674:1, qa:icadb-book:382:17]].
3. Giving charity (Zakat), which involves giving a portion of one's wealth to the needy [[qa:dorar-feqhia:2094:1, qa:icadb:36237]].
4. Fasting during the month of Ramadan [[qa:icadb-book:382:17, qa:dorar-feqhia:2094:1]].
5. Performing the pilgrimage (Hajj) to the House of Allah for those who are able to do so [[qa:icadb-book:382:17, qa:icadb:36237]].

